# Karpathy behavioral guidelines

When writing, reviewing, or refactoring code, first use the personal skill:

`~/.cursor/skills/karpathy-guidelines/SKILL.md`

Prefer this behavior by default:
- Think before coding (state assumptions, surface tradeoffs, ask when unclear).
- Keep solutions simple (minimum code that solves the requested problem).
- Make surgical changes (touch only what is necessary for the request).
- Use goal-driven execution (define verifiable success criteria and verify).